{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker(store:)"},{"text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"text":". A segment is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A store keeps only the event types you list in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CBOR (RFC 8949), each event a map of its properties under their names, written with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" and read with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryDecoder","type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance for you; write it by hand for an event declared without the macro. Events of other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types are delivered in this run but never written.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each drop is reported on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": the oldest segments","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set. Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRDBPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Persistence","import Trackers","","extension SignedUp: BinaryCodable {","    func encode(to encoder: inout BinaryEncoder) {","        encoder.encodeMap { map in","            map.encode(plan, forKey: \"plan\")","            map.encode(seats, forKey: \"seats\")","        }","    }","","    init(from decoder: inout BinaryDecoder) throws(BinaryDecodingError) {","        var map = try decoder.decodeMap()","        plan = try map.decode(forKey: \"plan\")","        seats = try map.decode(forKey: \"seats\", default: 1)","    }","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self], directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"anchor":"Stores","title":"Stores"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documen